      "content": "**Troubleshooting Guide: VPN Connection Timeout**\n\nExperiencing a VPN Connection Timeout can be frustrating, especially when you're trying to log in from home. This clear, step-by-step guide will help you resolve the issue effectively, but if these steps don't work for you, follow the detailed instructions below.\n\n1. **Check Your Internet Connection**\n   - Ensure your home internet connection is stable and working correctly.\n   - Try using another device to see if it has an internet connection.\n\n2. **Restart Your Router**\n   - Turn off your modem and router. Wait about 60 seconds. Power them back on and reconnect your device.\n   - Sometimes restarting your equipment can resolve connectivity issues.\n\n3. **Verify VPN Server Status**\n   - Check if the VPN server is online. Visit the helpdesk portal and look for any server outage notifications.\n   - If all VPN servers are online, try another available server in a different region/bandwidth option.\n  \n4. **Update Router Firmware**\n   - Make sure your router firmware is up to date. Consult your router's manual for instructions on checking and updating firmware.\n   - Old firmware may have bugs that could affect VPN connectivity.\n\n5. **Disable Firewall/Intrusion Prevention Systems (IPS",
